dsh-restart-client README · As a regular DSH bundle：Point a profile at the package directory:

```jsonc
// <profile>/package.json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "dsh-restart-client": "link:E:/path/to/dsh-restart-client"

Then restart the client once (by hand the first time — the button does not exist yet), and refresh the page after any `client.js` edit, since the desktop serves client halves from disk.

dsh-restart-client README · How the no-console restart works：If WSH is unavailable, the plugin falls back to creating the helper directly, so restarting still works even if a console flashes. A dry run reports which route would be taken:

```jsonc
// POST /api/dsh-restart/restart  {"dryRun": true}
{ "launch": "wscript (windowless)", ... }
```

dsh-restart-client README · `GET /api/dsh-restart/status`：```jsonc
{
  "ok": true,
  "host": { "platform": "win32", "selfPid": 26488, "desktopPid": 12724, "desktopOwned": true, "modes": ["client", "service"] }
}
